    historyContent: {
      origins: "Knock Poker emerged in the United States in the early 20th century as a non-gambling alternative to traditional poker. It was documented in Albert Ostrow's 'The Complete Card Player' (1945) and later in Scarne's 'Encyclopedia of Games' (1973).",
      originCountries: [
